    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Track---Field-Assistant-Coach_R-0000003585": {
      "title": "Track & Field Assistant Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003585 Position Title: Track & Field Assistant Coach Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $20.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 10/01/2026 Job Description: Mount Holyoke College, a highly respected member of NCAA Division III, is seeking a passionate, knowledgeable, and dedicated individual to join our Athletics department as a Part-Time Assistant Track & Field Coach. This is an exciting opportunity to help shape a dynamic student-athlete community by fostering both athletic excellence and personal growth within a competitive, inclusive, and values-driven program. The Assistant Coach will collaborate closely with the Head Coach and student leaders, supporting all aspects of program administration throughout the academic year. This role requires availability for evening and weekend commitments for practices, competitions, and recruiting events. Key Responsibilities: Coach assigned event groups during practices and competitions (throws experience strongly preferred). Ensure all training sessions and competitive environments adhere to proper safety standards and best practices within the sport. Assist the Head Coach with recruiting efforts, including communicating with prospective student-athletes in full compliance with NCAA Division III regulations. Support and help monitor the academic progress, personal development, and overall well-being of all track & field student-athletes. Assist with the maintenance, organization, and inventory of event-specific equipment. Contribute to the planning and execution of home track & field meets and events. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Required Qualifications: Commitment to supporting and developing student-athletes. Passion for the sport and dedication to athlete development. Strong attention to detail and excellent organizational skills. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Self-motivated, with the ability to teach and coach highly talented scholar-athletes in a rigorous academic environment. Demonstrated cultural competence working with a diverse student body. Valid driver’s license. Current Red Cross First Aid and CPR certification. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Knowledge of track & field (throws experience preferred). Competitive track & field experience. Previous coaching experience. Hire Rate: $20.00 / Hour Full Job Description Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Estate-and-Gift-Planning-Administrator_R-0000003619": {
      "title": "Estate and Gift Planning Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003619 Position Title: Estate and Gift Planning Administrator Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Full time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: Hybrid Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $28.48 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 10/26/2026 Job Description: Position Summary The Gift Planning Administrator manages the end-to-end operational and administrative workflow for the College's gift planning program. Acting as the primary liaison between donors, legal representatives, and internal teams, this role ensures the precise administration, recording, and stewardship of estates, trusts, and life income gifts. Key Responsibilities Estate & Trust Administration: Serve as the main point of contact for attorneys, executors, and the Alum Association. Review legal estate documents, monitor probate status, secure authorized signatures, and maintain precise records in the CRM database throughout the settlement process. Gift Processing & Compliance: Prepare life income gift contracts, financial illustrations, and tax disclosures. Process gifts-in-kind, relay confidential data to external custodians (e.g., TIAA Kaspick), and partner with the Finance Office to ensure accurate accounting and ledger coding. Donor Relations & Office Support: Act as the first point of contact for donor inquiries via phone and email. Manage office budget tracking, expense reporting, cross-departmental scheduling, file management, and event support (such as Reunion and Commencement). Core Qualifications Associate’s degree with a minimum of one year of job-related office experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience with estate/trust administration, paralegal workflows, or gift planning operations. Proficiency in database management (CRM) and office budget tracking. Exceptional communication skills with a proven track record of handling sensitive financial data with empathy, discretion, and strict confidentiality. Please review the Full Job Description Starting Range: $28.48 - $35.58 per hour Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
