    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Lyons-Lift-Driver_R-0000003537": {
      "title": "Lyons Lift Driver",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003537 Position Title: Lyons Lift Driver Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $21.87 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 09/28/2026 Job Description: Lyons Lift drivers support individuals with permanent or temporary mobility limitations with rides on campus, ensuring them safe and friendly access to classes, dining, and other campus locations, as well as the Village Commons. Driver shifts start at 7:45am through the early afternoon Mondays through Thursdays throughout the semester. Shifts are primarily spent in the van providing rides based on the schedule for that day as well as fielding calls to schedule additional rides as-needed. Primary responsibilities include safe operation of vehicles on shift, effective management of ride scheduling, knowledge of campus pickup locations, comfort working with people with disabilities, and maintaining a helpful, kind, and safety-forward attitude while engaging with student riders. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Ensure the safe transportation of individuals on route Assist individuals entering and exiting the vehicle as needed Possess knowledge of relevant ADA guidelines and familiarity with ramp deployment and wheelchair securement technology Provide curb-to-curb service in a professional, safe, and courteous manner Conduct and document vehicle safety checks before each shift Maintain punctuality for rides on shift Manage scheduling with passengers during shifts Report and record all incidents to Public Safety Dispatch and document for the Lyons Lift Supervisor Maintain confidentiality and professionalism Keep vehicle clean and free of trash Record daily ridership records Communicate with the direct supervisor any issues or concerns Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications: You must be a fleet-certified driver or able to become certified Valid driver’s license (any state) and satisfactory driving record (no violations within the last year) Satisfactory criminal background check and drug/alcohol screen may be required Embraces and actively promotes an inclusive and equitable environment for all members of the MHC community Ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Call volume can be very high before and after classes, as well as during bad weather Preferred Qualifications: Excellent interpersonal skills, pleasant and friendly demeanor Demonstrates ability to work independently Experience working with people with disabilities and people with mobility limitations. Demonstrates skill in understanding cultural differences Strengthens Mount Holyoke College’s climate for inclusion and acceptance Embraces and actively promotes an includes and equitable work environment Hiring Range: $21.87 - $24.05 Full Job Description What We Offer: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Assistant-Basketball-Coach_R-0000003553": {
      "title": "Assistant Basketball Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003553 Position Title: Assistant Basketball Coach Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $20.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 10/15/2026 Job Description: The Part-Time Assistant Basketball Coach provides on-court, operational, and instructional support to the intercollegiate basketball program during the competitive season. This position focuses primarily on student-athlete development, daily practice execution, game-day preparation, and strategy implementation. This is a non-recruiting, seasonal role tailored to active team operations. This position contributes to the College’s mission by fostering a diverse, inclusive, and supportive environment that empowers student-athletes to grow as individuals, competitors, and leaders. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: On-Court Coaching & Practice Execution: Assist the head coach in organizing, planning, and conducting daily practices, including executing training programs and skill development for assigned positional groups. Game Preparation & In-Game Management: Support the head coach in developing game strategies, preparing scouting briefs, and managing bench strategy and adjustments during contests. In-Season Team Operations: Attend and support team needs at all in-season practices, team meetings, and contests (both home and away). Student-Athlete Development: Create an inclusive team environment that fosters a positive culture of health, well-being, and safety, allowing student-athletes to grow as students, athletes, leaders, and individuals. Cultural Alignment: Support and execute the head coach’s vision, philosophy, and strategic plan by consistently reinforcing the team's cultural standards. Other Duties: Perform additional in-season, team-focused duties as assigned by the head coach. Required Qualifications: BA/BS Collegiate coaching  The ability to foster positive relationships with student-athletes and promote a positive team culture at a competitive liberal arts college with highly selective academic standards. Member of the NEWMAC and NCAA Division III. CPR/AED certification Valid drivers license  Preferred Qualifications: MA/MS   Hire rate: $20.00 / Hour Full Job Description Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Music-Instructor_R-0000003532": {
      "title": "Music Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003532 Position Title: Music Instructor Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $0.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: Job Description: The Mount Holyoke College Department of Music seeks Music Instructors to teach Individual Performance Study (ie. music lessons) for interested students. Instructors are on the active roster for lessons in their instrument(s), though the total number of billable teaching hours each semester is subject, as always, to student enrollments. Our Music Instructors teach students at all levels, from beginner to advanced, across a range of voice types and instruments. Individual Performance Study is one of the requirements for the Music major, supports excellence in our many department ensembles, and is also very popular with non-majors/minors. Lessons are one of the few instructional areas where a student can experience sustained one-on-one teaching, and may have the same instructor each semester for their entire undergraduate career. We therefore prize Music Instructors who cultivate welcoming, respectful, and supportive studios; offer students a diverse range of repertoire; prioritize wellness and sustainable approaches to technique; and help students develop pathways for a lifetime of thoughtful engagement with music, whatever their future professional goals may be. This is an academic-year, non-benefited appointment (September 1 - May 31), renewable annually.  Important Application Note: This is a Rolling Application. We are continuously recruiting talent for our future needs. Submitting an application puts your information directly into our active pool, and we will contact you for an interview should a suitable opening become available. Submitting an application does not guarantee an opening. Instruments currently offered: Piano Voice Flute Oboe Clarinet Saxophone Bassoon French Horn Trumpet - Currently Searching for Trumpet Instructor (for AY26-27) Trombone Tuba Percussion Harpsichord Organ Harp Guitar Electric Guitar Violin Viola Cello Double Bass Electric Bass Early instruments: Lute, Viola da Gamba, Recorders, etc. Essential Responsibilities: Offer 10 30-minute or 60-minute lessons per student per semester, depending on the number of credits and student enrollments Assist students with placement and enrollment Prepare and distribute syllabi Prepare for lessons Assist students in preparing for end-of-semester performances and half or full recitals Assist students with mentorship and musical opportunities as appropriate Submit grades Qualifications: Master’s degree in Music Minimum one year prior experience teaching one-on-one private music lessons Commitment to Mount Holyoke College’s climate of academic excellence and inclusive learning within our gender-diverse women’s liberal arts college environment Compensation: $ 73.54/HR for lessons and $36.78/HR for administrative work Special Instructions for Applicants: Apply online; application materials must include: A cover letter summarizing interests and qualifications A complete resume or curriculum vitae Links to at least two videos of you in performance for each instrument you teach, recorded within the last 5 years Encouraged but not required: one or more videos of you teaching your instrument, recorded within the last 5 years Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Stable-Assistant_R-0000003243": {
      "title": "Stable Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003243 Position Title: Stable Assistant Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $21.87 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 10/05/2026 Job Description: The Stable Assistant supports the daily operations of the Mount Holyoke College Equestrian Center by providing high-quality care for horses and maintaining the cleanliness, safety, and organization of the stables. This role is essential in fostering a welcoming and professional environment for students, boarders, and visitors, while ensuring the health and well-being of the college’s equine partners. Schedule: Wednesday: 10AM-6PM Saturday: 10AM-6PM Sunday: 10AM-6PM Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Essential Worker (all weather and holidays) Provide hay and fresh water to horses Feed horses according to individualized grain cards and administer supplements Track supplement inventory and notify boarders or stable manager when supplies are low Turn out and bring in horses on a rotational schedule Clean and maintain horse stalls (10–13 daily, with occasional additional needs) Sweep aisles, remove debris, and maintain a tidy appearance throughout the barn Clean and maintain wash stalls, drains, and water tubs Remove trash and replace bags Conduct regular cobwebbing and dusting Move and organize feed, hay, and bedding as needed Muck paddocks and rake hay or leaves from surrounding areas Operate barn equipment such as tractors and manure wagons Assist with regular maintenance projects and seasonal preparations Examples: dragging arenas, raking walkways, dusting knee-walls, and prepping for returning boarders Work collaboratively with other barn staff to ensure smooth daily operations Read the Stable log and check the Daily staff schedule before every shift Communicate regularly with the associate director regarding horse care and facility needs Required Qualifications: Previous horse handling, husbandry, and general farm experience. Must be able to work both independently as well as on a team. Ability to operate and learn google sheets and forms. Preferred Qualifications: Experience operating a tractor and farm equipment. Experience with dragging an arena and general arena maintenance. Equine first aid and emergency knowledge. Experience working at an equine boarding facility Experience working in a lesson barn. Hiring Range: $ 21.87 - $24.05 What We Offer: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Italian_R-0000003517-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Italian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003517 Position Title: Assistant Professor of Italian Work Type: Faculty   Full time   In-Person Start Date: 07/01/2027 Job Description: The Department of Classics and Italian at Mount Holyoke College and the Department of German and Italian at Smith College invite applications for a joint tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Italian with a specialization in Medieval, Renaissance, and/or Early Modern Studies, starting July 1, 2027. The successful candidate will teach four courses/year split between the two campuses (two at Mount Holyoke and two at Smith). We especially welcome candidates whose work engages Transnational Italian Studies, Mediterranean Studies, Global Early Modern Studies, digital humanities, visual and material culture, environmental humanities, race and ethnicity, and/or  migration studies. We seek a colleague with a strong research and teaching record. The successful candidate will teach language, culture, and literature courses with broad interdisciplinary appeal, and will contribute to collaborations across the Five Colleges. The ability to teach both in Italian and in English is essential. PhD or ABD required. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of strong teaching at the undergraduate level and experience mentoring students who are broadly diverse with regard to race, ethnicity, socioeconomic status, gender, nationality, sexual orientation, and religion. In addition to the teaching load, expectations for the successful candidate include maintaining an active research program, mentoring and advising students through honors projects, special studies, and other independent research. Candidates will be required to submit, in addition to CV with the names of three referees, a letter of application, and writing sample not exceeding 20 pages, three statements (not exceeding one page each) concerning (1) teaching philosophy, (2) research interests, and (3) a statement about mentoring a diverse student body. Candidates should submit these materials by December 7, 2026. Three reference letters will be requested at a later date in the process. Questions may be addressed to Denise Falk, Department Coordinator, Department of Classics and Italian, Mount Holyoke College at dfalk@mthoyloke.edu . Minimum starting rate of pay: $90,000. Mount Holyoke and Smith Colleges are undergraduate liberal arts colleges with over 2000 students each. They are located about 90 miles west of Boston in the Connecticut River valley, and are members of the Five College Consortium consisting of Amherst, Hampshire, Mount Holyoke, and Smith Colleges and the University of Massachusetts. They are women’s colleges that are gender diverse. The Colleges are committed to providing equal access and opportunity in employment and education to all employees and students. In compliance with state and federal law, Mount Holyoke College and Smith College do not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, genetic information, sex, national or ethnic origin, religion, age, physical or mental disability, marital status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, ancestry, veteran or military status, or any other legally protected status under federal, state or local law.    Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Cook_R-0000003423": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003423 Position Title: Cook Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Full time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $28.76 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 08/24/2026 Job Description: Mount Holyoke College Dining Commons offers a diverse array of cuisines tailored to meet various dietary preferences and needs. Our menu frequently rotates to provide students, faculty, and staff with an expansive selection. Highlights include the customizable WOK station, offering personalized stir fry dishes, and the Baraka station, specializing is Halal cuisine. For those seeking Kosher options, the L’Chaim station is available. Our culinary team is dedicated to crafting nutritious, flavorful meals that cater to the diverse tastes of our students, faculty, and staff. We prioritize safety and sanitation in all meal preparations. In addition to Vegan and Vegetarian options, we strive to create an inclusive dining environment where every person, despite their dietary needs, can enjoy healthy and delicious foods. Essential Job Functions: Preparation of recipes while ensuring safe handling and proper food preparation techniques. Adherence to sanitation and Board of Health (BOH) regulations, including proper receiving and storage procedures. Record daily temperatures of all food items and maintain production records to ensure food safety, compliance with BOH regulations. Complete administrative tasks such as providing accurate information for menu planning and inventory management on a daily basis. Collaboration with culinary team members to facilitate smooth and efficient operations. Food preparation using methods such as boiling, roasting, sautéing, steaming, baking, frying, and grilling/broiling. Assurance of accurate allergen information and ingredient labeling. Consistent use of standardized recipes to maintain food quality and presentation. Implementation of inventory management practices, including regular inventory counts and First in, First out (FIFO) method utilization. Proper maintenance of cooking equipment and up-keep a clean and organized workspace. Qualifications : Minimum of 2 years of experience in high-volume food preparation. Ability to pass a pre-employment physical examination without restrictions. Must possess strong written and verbal communication skills. ServSafe certification or willingness to obtain certification. Certification in allergen training or willingness to obtain one. Commitment to exceptional customer service and professionalism. Preferred Qualifications : Preference of 3 years of experience in high-volume food preparation, preferably in a higher education setting or quality restaurant setting. Proficiency in basic computer skills. Entry Rate $28.87 - Working Rate $30.66 Dining Video Please note that this position falls under a Union, which ensures fair compensation and benefits for all employees. What We Offer: Our comprehensive benefits program offers a range of options to you can make choices that work best for you and your family: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Cashier_R-0000003148": {
      "title": "Cashier",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003148 Position Title: Cashier Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $19.89 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 03/30/2026 Job Description: The Dining Services Department is seeking a Cashier to provide excellent customer service while accurately processing payments through cash, One Cards, and debit/credit cards. This role includes managing the checkout process efficiently, handling transactions in a timely manner, and maintaining a clean and organized work environment. Cashiers will also be responsible for cleaning and sanitizing dining areas to ensure a pleasant and hygienic experience for all guests. Essential Responsibilities:  Responsible for the operation of the computerized point of sale system. Monitor meal plan transactions closely to ensure the student has appropriate balance. Assists in stocking and cleaning throughout the dining commons. Must be able to work with others, including students, as well as work alone without supervision. Assists in supervision and training of student workers. Keeps all work areas clean, free of debris and sanitized at all times. At times, will provide direction to student staff and needs to maintain a high level of professionalism. Oversees the distribution and return of takeout containers and travel mugs. Performs other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Cash handling experience and proficiency in math. Good communication skills, both written and orally, with a sound understanding of the English language. Should maintain an extraordinarily positive attitude in dealing with students and the public. Attention to detail, excellent communication skills, and the ability to work well in a fast-paced environment. Minimum starting hourly rate for this position is $ 19.89 This role is classified under Hourly Grade 4H with an hourly ran ge between $19.89 - $21.87 / hour What We Offer: Our comprehensive benefits program offers a range of options to you can make choices that work best for you and your family: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
