    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/PTOC-Lyons-Lift-Driver_R-0000003494": {
      "title": "PTOC Lyons Lift Driver",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003494 Position Title: PTOC Lyons Lift Driver Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $19.50 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 08/24/2026 Job Description: Part Time On-Call Driver for Lyons Lift, Mount Holyoke's on-campus accessible ride program The Lyons Lift program at Mount Holyoke College is looking for a part time on-call employee to join our team at Public Safety and Services . Lyons Lift Drivers operate our wheelchair accessible van to support individuals with permanent or temporary mobility limitations with rides on campus, ensuring them safe and friendly access to classes, dining, and other campus locations, as well as the Village Commons. In this role, you would be asked to work coverage shifts as needed and for special events. Ensure the safe transportation of individuals on route  Assist individuals entering and exiting the vehicle as needed Provide curb-to-curb service in a professional, safe, and courteous manner Conduct and document vehicle safety checks before each shift Manage scheduling with passengers during shifts  Report and record all incidents to Public Safety Dispatch and document for the Lyons Lift Supervisor. Maintain confidentiality and professionalism Keep vehicle clean and free of trash Record daily ridership records Communicate with the direct supervisor any issues or concerns Qualifications: You must be a fleet-certified driver or able to become certified  Valid driver’s license (any state) and satisfactory driving record (no violations within the last year)  Ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Call volume can be very high before and after classes, as well as during bad weather  Ability to assist individuals in and out of vehicles Excellent interpersonal skills, pleasant and friendly demeanor Ability to communicate effectively with riders and supervisors  Demonstrated ability to work independently Must be available to attend all meetings and training sessions Satisfactory criminal background check and drug/alcohol screen may be required All drivers and riders must wear seat belts. No cell phone usage or any other distractions while driving  Safety check of the vehicle before and after each shift.  Ability to safely refuel the vehicle at MHC pump Full Job Description Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Director-of-Admission-Systems-and-Operations_R-0000003485": {
      "title": "Director of Admission Systems and Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003485 Position Title: Director of Admission Systems and Operations Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Full time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: Hybrid Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $95,318.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 10/01/2026 Job Description: Under the supervision of the Dean of Admission, the Director of Systems &amp; Operations oversees the development, execution, support, and evaluation of a robust and comprehensive CRM system, working with senior enrollment leadership and colleagues across campus to help them effectively utilize technology within their respective areas of responsibility. The Director focuses the department on innovation, efficiency, and industry-leading technology practices, ensuring the infrastructure and service quality needed for smooth management of the overall admission operation, which receives roughly 6,000 applications annually and operates first year, transfer, and Frances Perkins admission processes. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Serve as the Slate Captain and primary CRM subject matter expert, overseeing system administration, workflows, user access, and project implementation. Act as the Office of Admission's data steward, managing data governance and collaborating with vendors, campus partners, and admission staff. Represent Admission on Workday CRM and ERP integration initiatives, ensuring departmental needs are prioritized and supporting future platform integrations. Develop business continuity protocols to ensure operational resilience and data integrity. Monitor industry trends and implement strategies that enhance admission systems, operations, and organizational effectiveness. Develop, implement, and review policies and procedures that support departmental goals and continuous improvement. Lead systems and operations functions to ensure efficient, integrated processes across the department. Recruit, supervise, coach, and evaluate staff while fostering professional development and high-quality service. Promote communication, collaboration, and knowledge sharing across the department. Use data analytics and visualization tools to assess performance, support reporting, and inform strategic decision-making. Represent the Office of Admission on institutional committees and data governance initiatives, serving as a key cross-functional partner. SKILLS/ KNOWLEDGE/ CERTIFICATIONS: 1. Required Bachelor's degree; a minimum of 7 years of experience in admission or a related field. Ability to work collegially with a diverse group of students, faculty, staff, and visitors on a daily basis. Superior oral, analytic, and written communication skills; effective public speaking; an ability to engage with large audiences of prospective students, families, and college counselors. Deep experience with and knowledge of Technolutions Slate CRM. Expert competency in Google Suite and Microsoft Office. Ability to use data to make strategic decisions. An understanding of the liberal arts and an ability to communicate its value in a gender-diverse women's college context clearly, cogently, and confidently. Sense of humor and ability to remain flexible and nimble in carrying out multiple projects and tasks.   2. Preferred Master's degree; 10 years of experience in technology management, admission, or enrollment management with progressively increasing levels of responsibility. Experience working in a selective college/university admission environment. Knowledge about and passion for women's colleges and gender-affirming communities.       Full Job Description Please upload resume and cover letter Hiring Range: $ 95,318.00 - $142,977.00 Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Diving-Coach_R-0000003253": {
      "title": "Diving Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003253 Position Title: Diving Coach Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $20.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 09/01/2026 Job Description: This is a part-time, seasonal position reporting to the Head Swimming and Diving Coach. The Assistant Coach is responsible for assisting in all aspects of a competitive NCAA Division III varsity diving program. The primary focus is the instruction, safety, and recruitment of student-athletes within the diving discipline. This role requires a commitment to the mission of Mount Holyoke College, fostering a diverse and inclusive environment that supports the holistic development of scholar-athletes. The position includes evening and weekend hours and follows the academic calendar. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Lead all diving practices, meets, and dryland activities. Provide technical analysis of performance, identifying areas for improvement and teaching new dives and techniques using specialized equipment (e.g., trampoline and spotting rig). Ensure all activities adhere to industry safety standards. Maintain a thorough knowledge of and compliance with NCAA Division III and Mount Holyoke College regulations regarding recruiting, student-athlete eligibility, and PSA (Prospective Student-Athlete) evaluations. Manage the full lifecycle of diving recruitment. Identify, evaluate, and communicate with PSAs to build a competitive roster of student-athletes. Oversee the academic progress and personal well-being of swimming and diving student-athletes, serving as a mentor and resource. Assist the Head Coach with administrative tasks, including travel logistics, meal arrangements, fundraising initiatives, and home meet management. Maintain and oversee the upkeep of diving-specific equipment (boards, harnesses, trampolines) to ensure a safe and high-functioning training environment. Maintain a working knowledge of e-Dive, Dive Meet, and other relevant recruiting or department software. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Commitment to the student-athlete, passion for the sport, and a high degree of self-motivation to recruit and coach in a challenging academic environment. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with a diverse student body and a commitment to fostering an inclusive team culture. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills with the ability to communicate effectively with students, staff, and prospective families. Ability to safely use a trampoline and spotting rig for training and instructive purposes. Current Red Cross First Aid and CPR certification. Valid driver’s license.   Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Previous coaching experience Competitive diving experience. Lifeguard Training Certification. Full Job Description Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Club-Sports-Coach---Part-Time_R-0000003028": {
      "title": "Club Sports Coach - Part-Time",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003028 Position Title: Club Sports Coach - Part-Time Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $20.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 08/01/2026 Job Description: Mount Holyoke College’s Athletics Department is seeking part-time Club Coaches to guide our dedicated student-athletes. This is more than just coaching; it’s fostering athletic excellence, leadership development, and personal growth within a collaborative club sports environment. If you have a passion for your sport and a commitment to mentorship, this is your chance to coach a team of motivated, bright student leaders. Important Application Note: This is a Rolling Application. We are continuously recruiting talent for our future needs. Submitting an application puts your information directly into our active pool, and we will contact you for an interview should a suitable opening becomes available. Submitting an application does not guarantee an immediate opening. Why be a Club Coach at MHC? You’ll be a direct mentor to exceptional student athletes, helping them shape their athletic and leadership journeys. This role requires approximately 6-8 hours per week during the academic year, primarily during weekday evenings. It’s the perfect opportunity for local experts, recent graduates, or passionate individuals seeking involvement outside of a standard 9-to-5. You'll work closely with student-run club boards, collaborating on decisions and fostering an inclusive team culture. Club Sports currently offered:  Fencing Rugby Ultimate Frisbee Ice Hockey - Currently Searching for Head & Assistant Club Coaches Squash Dressage Western Essential Duties and Responsibilities:  Designing and executing engaging, high-quality practices focused on fundamentals, strategy, conditioning, and safety. Mentoring student leaders and collaborating with them on team vision and day-to-day decisions. Championing an inclusive team culture that supports the holistic growth (academic, athletic, and personal) of every student-athlete. Ensuring safety by supervising drills, maintaining equipment, and upholding all facility and departmental policies. Supporting the team at all practices and competitions (potential weeknight and weekend flexibility required). Listed as the PE Club Course Instructor and certify PE credits in collaboration with the Assistant Athletic Director. Qualifications: Proven experience playing and/or coaching your sport. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills – you can clearly teach a technique and motivate a group. A commitment to diversity and inclusion and the ability to support an environment where all student-athletes feel valued. Familiarity with the rules, trends, and compliance requirements within your sport. Must be able to work weeknights/weekends as needed and possess a valid driver’s license. Hiring Range: $20.00 - $30.00/hr. Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
